# Validate with: cffconvert --validate
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, its results or its figures, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "urban-functional-maps: open mobility data for functional-area maps"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible pipeline, paper and slides on what open mobility sources leave out
  (origin-destination pairs, trip purpose, time of day) and on how much of a functional-area
  map is produced by scale, contiguity and construction. Census commuting matrices of England
  and Wales (2011, 2021), Dutch register jobs between municipalities (2023), Spanish trips
  between districts from operator data (2023), Serbian census bands (2022), the Japanese
  people-flow panel and OpenStreetMap GPS traces. Contains a closed form for the permutation
  null of partition self-containment, a recombination Markov chain for contiguous partitions
  of the same sizes, the Coombes-Bond algorithm (R package LabourMarketAreas) with the
  parameters of the official Travel to Work Areas, and a spatial error matrix with
  intersection over union against official regions.
